 },
 "blocks": [
  {
   "id": "t0",
   "kind": "h",
   "text": "Ethereum",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 90,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 44
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t1",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "Ethereum is a decentralized blockchain with smart contract functionality. Ether (ETH) is the native cryptocurrency of the platform. Among cryptocurrencies, ether is second only to bitcoin in market capitalization.",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 160,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 44
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t2",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "In 2022, Ethereum transitioned its consensus mechanism from proof-of-work (PoW) to proof-of-stake (PoS) in an update known as the Merge, which reduced Ethereum's energy usage by 99%.",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 230,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 44
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t3",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "The idea of Ethereum was proposed by Vitalik Buterin in late 2013. Development was crowdfunded in 2014, and the network went live on 30 July 2015.",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 300,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 44
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t4",
   "kind": "h",
   "text": "History",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 370,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 44
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t5",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "Ethereum was conceived in 2013 by programmer Vitalik Buterin. Additional founders of Ethereum included Gavin Wood, Charles Hoskinson, Anthony Di Iorio and Joseph Lubin.",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 440,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 44
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t6",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "In 2016, a smart contract called The DAO was exploited, and about 3.6 million ether was drained. The community chose a hard fork to reverse it, which created Ethereum Classic from the chain that did not fork.",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 510,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 44
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t7",
   "kind": "h",
   "text": "Design",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 580,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 44
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t8",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "Ethereum's code is run on the Ethereum Virtual Machine (EVM), and smart contracts are mostly written in Solidity. Users pay gas, denominated in gwei, to run transactions.",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 650,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 44
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t9",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "Staking requires 32 ETH per validator. Validators propose and attest to blocks and can be penalised (slashed) for misbehaviour.",
   "inView": false,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 720,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 44
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t10",
   "kind": "h",
   "text": "Applications",
   "inView": false,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 790,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 44
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t11",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "Applications on Ethereum include decentralized finance (DeFi), non-fungible tokens (NFTs) and stablecoins.",
   "inView": false,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 860,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 44
   }
  }
 ],
